  "hindi": "यह पहला यहाँ धारण करने वालों द्वारा स्थापित किया गया है, होता, सर्वश्रेष्ठ यजन करने वाला, यज्ञों में स्तुति के योग्य; जिसे अप्नवान और भृगुओं ने वनों में चमकाया, विचित्र और व्यापक को, प्रत्येक जनसमुदाय के लिए।",
  "english": "This first one has been placed here by the placers, the Hotṛ priest, the best sacrificer, to be praised in the rites; whom Apnavāna and the Bhṛgus made shine in the woods, the wondrous, the pervasive, for every clan.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "dhātṛ \"placer, establisher\" (agent noun of √dhā). apnavānaḥ is singular and stands before bhṛgavaḥ; taken as a name beside the Bhṛgus (it could also be read as an epithet qualifying them). virurucuḥ is a perfect of √ruc used here with causative sense (\"made shine\"). viśe-viśe is distributive dative \"for each clan\". The relative clause continues in the grammar of 4.7.1 only; no verb is left unexpressed.",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
