  "hindi": "हे अग्नि, तुम्हारा, देव का, ध्यान कब निरन्तर होगा? तब ही तो मनुष्यों ने जनसमुदायों में तुम्हें, स्तुति के योग्य को, पकड़ लिया है।",
  "english": "O Agni, when will your attention, that of the god, be continuous? For then mortals have seized you, the one to be praised, among the clans.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "ta = te (gen.), \"your\"; devasya \"of the god\" stands in apposition to te. cetanam (from √cit) is rendered \"attention, noticing\"; the sense of the first line is not fully clear (alternatives: \"the god's appearing\", \"awareness\"). anuṣak is taken as \"in succession, continuously\". adhā hi \"for then/now\".",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
