  "hindi": "वैवस्वत के तीव्र दूत को, जो सब जनों के ऊपर है; आयुओं ने पताका को, भृगु जैसे को, प्रत्येक जनसमुदाय के लिए लाया।",
  "english": "The swift messenger of Vivasvat, who is over all the peoples; the Āyus brought hither the banner, the Bhṛgu-like one, for every clan.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The sentence continues from 4.7.3 (paśyantaḥ ... jabhruḥ): \"seeing him ... they brought\". abhi with the accusative has no verb of its own; \"over\" is chosen, \"towards\" is possible. āyavaḥ is taken as a plural \"Āyus, men\" (the sense of the word as a tribe or as \"living men\" is not settled). bhṛgavāṇam \"Bhṛgu-like\" (an -āṇa formation); its exact sense and whether it agrees with ketum or with Agni is not certain. Hindi renders viś as जनसमुदाय.",
